     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am following this example to upload and analyze csv files with R:<br><a href=\"http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/file-upload.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/file-upload.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792397230599000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2YTvvSzqKZE84C_zXZ_G4H\">http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/file-upload.html</a><br><br>I have two general questions about file upload with Shiny.<br><br>1. Can I use the same file to create multiple outputs, without having to read it each time?<br>So far, my code looks like this. As you can see, I am reading the same file three times. When I try to read the file only once before the output functions, I get an error, but I feel there has to be a more elegant way to handle this.<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">shinyServer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br>  output$densityPlot </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderPlot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>    inFile </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> input$file1<br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#008\">null</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inFile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NULL</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">File</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">inFile$datapath</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">File</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">File</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># switch axis to be consistent</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br>    withProgress</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">message </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;flowDensity&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> value </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    result </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> runDensity</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">File</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\